0 Toggle Lever — crank, Scotch yoke and a link folding toward dead centre
0 Name: toggle-lever.ldr
0 Author: CrispStrobe
0 !LICENSE BSD-3-Clause : see ../licenses/toggle-lever.txt
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 // One fixed SPIKE Prime hub and one medium angular motor on A.
0 // Reused SineShuttle base/yoke frame (BSD-3-Clause, CrispStrobe). Built from the
0 // automated builder bw-opencode-mfg-r2-20261025's ToggleJaw, re-layered so that no
0 // two bodies interpenetrate: lever pivoted at its end hole on top, link above it.
0 // Horizontal yoke and lever: gravity gives no starting torque.
0 // Saved datum: crank pin at +X, lever input arm at +36.87 deg.
0 // Law (LDU, plan view): yoke pin Y = (40 cos theta, 100); pivot P = (0, 120);
0 // lever arm |PL| = 20; link |YL| = 40; tip on the same line at 40 from P.
0 // The link folds over the pivot (dead centre) at theta = 90; the program stops at 85.
0 // Assembly: 01 — reused frame, feet, hub, motor cradle

